  "user_request_original": "Design a 24-layer planar multilayer dielectric film on fused silica substrate with air incident medium. Use only hfo2 and SiO2 (Lemarchand) materials in alternating sequence starting with hfo2 at the air interface. Optimize individual layer thicknesses with bounds constrained to 65-105 nm. Initialize with quarter-wave optical thickness pattern centered at 550 nm (hfo2 approximately 69 nm, SiO2 (Lemarchand) approximately 95 nm). Reduce learning rate by 50% compared to prior optimization round. Increase regularization penalty on inter-layer thickness variance. Evaluate performance at normal incidence across two wavelength bands: maximize transmittance in 1530-1565 nm band and maximize reflectance in 400-700 nm band. Total layer count fixed at 24.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize 24 alternating HfO2 and SiO2 layers on a fused silica substrate with air incidence. Fix the sequence to start with HfO2 and bound all layer thicknesses between 65 and 105 nm, initializing to quarter-wave optical thickness at 550 nm (approx. 69 nm HfO2, 95 nm SiO2). Reduce the optimizer learning rate to 0.025 and increase inter-layer thickness variance regularization. Evaluate performance at normal incidence by maximizing average transmittance in the 1530–1565 nm band and maximizing average reflectance in the 400–700 nm band.",
